WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.580 --> 00:00:01.770
Meet Lobo.

00:00:01.770 --> 00:00:03.130
“Who are you?”

00:00:03.380 --> 00:00:08.160
“Oh, I’m sorry...my card.”

00:00:08.170 --> 00:00:14.849
He's basically a mashup of Superman and Wolverine:
an immortal, unkillable alien antihero that

00:00:14.849 --> 00:00:21.910
happens to have super senses, a crazy healing
factor, and a love for beer and cigars.

00:00:21.910 --> 00:00:23.460
Sounds great, right?

00:00:23.460 --> 00:00:25.519
Well, not so much.

00:00:25.519 --> 00:00:30.810
His biggest fans have waited years for Lobo
to make the jump to the silver screen — and

00:00:30.810 --> 00:00:37.330
the success of 2016's R-rated Deadpool seemed
to be proof that bawdier comic book characters

00:00:37.330 --> 00:00:40.000
would start heading to theaters in short order.

00:00:40.000 --> 00:00:45.310
But, really, chances are pretty good that
it just won't happen.

00:00:45.310 --> 00:00:47.070
“Mmm, I love you too.”

00:00:49.050 --> 00:00:55.160
Here's why DC and Warner Bros. will never
give Lobo his own movie.

00:00:55.160 --> 00:00:56.890
Parody problems

00:00:56.890 --> 00:01:02.580
The most fundamental problem with creating
a Lobo movie is that Lobo is, at heart, a

00:01:02.580 --> 00:01:03.690
parody.

00:01:03.690 --> 00:01:07.720
The character was first created by writer/artist
Keith Giffen.

00:01:07.720 --> 00:01:11.330
When asked why Lobo became so popular, Giffen
answered,

00:01:11.330 --> 00:01:13.740
"I have no idea why Lobo took off.

00:01:13.740 --> 00:01:20.300
I came up with him as an indictment of the
Punisher, Wolverine, bad ass hero prototype

00:01:20.300 --> 00:01:24.890
and somehow he caught on as the high violence
poster boy.

00:01:24.890 --> 00:01:25.890
Go figure."

00:01:25.890 --> 00:01:31.500
But even though he started as a parody, Lobo's
biggest fans didn't really get the joke.

00:01:31.500 --> 00:01:33.850
Or if they did, they didn't really care.

00:01:33.850 --> 00:01:36.970
Lobo became a legitimate fan favorite.

00:01:36.970 --> 00:01:42.390
But while Wolverine and the Punisher have
become iconic hits in both comics and on-screen,

00:01:42.390 --> 00:01:49.320
an accurate adaptation of Lobo today would
just come across as a cheap rip-off of Marvel's

00:01:49.320 --> 00:01:53.690
characters because…well…he kind of is.

00:01:53.690 --> 00:01:56.820
As Giffen said, that was the whole point.

00:01:56.820 --> 00:01:58.580
Too misogynistic

00:01:58.580 --> 00:02:03.050
One of Lobo's signature character traits has
been his sexism and misogyny.

00:02:03.050 --> 00:02:08.890
In one notable comic, he ripped the top off
of superheroine Starfire against her will

00:02:08.890 --> 00:02:11.380
as "payment" for his help.

00:02:11.380 --> 00:02:18.130
Now, if Lobo's nothing more than a parody,
this kind of thing is at least a little okay.

00:02:18.130 --> 00:02:22.270
His awfulness and boundary pushing is the
joke, right?

00:02:22.270 --> 00:02:27.450
But it's difficult to imagine that level of
casual sexism taking place in the same cinematic

00:02:27.450 --> 00:02:31.620
universe as Lois Lane and the new, butt-kicking
Wonder Woman.

00:02:31.620 --> 00:02:32.620
“You pig!

00:02:32.620 --> 00:02:33.620
Ow!”

00:02:33.620 --> 00:02:34.620
“Ahh!

00:02:34.620 --> 00:02:36.060
I like a babe who plays rough.”

00:02:36.060 --> 00:02:41.060
If nothing else, Lobo is a PR nightmare waiting
to happen.

00:02:41.060 --> 00:02:42.760
That whole genocide thing

00:02:42.760 --> 00:02:47.940
In most superhero stories, the hero is partially
defined by tragedy.

00:02:47.940 --> 00:02:53.099
That goes for Batman losing his parents, or
Superman losing his entire planet.

00:02:53.099 --> 00:02:58.640
These events shape their entire moral compass
and charts their course towards eventually

00:02:58.640 --> 00:03:00.500
putting on a cape.

00:03:00.500 --> 00:03:07.400
Lobo is literally the complete opposite: like
Superman, he's the last of his race.

00:03:07.400 --> 00:03:11.500
Unlike Superman, he didn't lose his home planet
in a moment of tragedy.

00:03:11.500 --> 00:03:15.840
Instead, he unleashed a plague that killed
his entire planet.

00:03:15.840 --> 00:03:17.680
"I'm the last Czarnian.

00:03:17.680 --> 00:03:20.980
I fragged the rest of the planet for my high
school science project.

00:03:20.980 --> 00:03:22.910
Gave myself an A."

00:03:22.910 --> 00:03:28.780
While we may cheer as Deadpool slices and
dices henchman, we know his victims are actually

00:03:28.780 --> 00:03:32.790
bad guys who contributed to a mutant trafficking
ring.

00:03:32.790 --> 00:03:38.180
Killing an entire planet, on the other hand,
is pretty over the top for most villains,

00:03:38.180 --> 00:03:41.770
let alone goofy antiheroes.

00:03:41.770 --> 00:03:43.209
Inconsistent power level

00:03:43.209 --> 00:03:48.760
One of the basic rules of storytelling is
that characters must somehow be vulnerable.

00:03:48.760 --> 00:03:54.150
This helps them face various crises and grow
over the course of a story.

00:03:54.150 --> 00:03:58.940
When superheroes have no apparent vulnerabilities,
you have to introduce something.

00:03:58.940 --> 00:04:04.020
That's one of the reasons why Superman's weakness
is Kryptonite: to bring him down to Earth.

00:04:04.020 --> 00:04:09.440
Lobo's powers are inconsistent at best, and
ridiculous at worst.

00:04:09.440 --> 00:04:14.989
He's literally unkillable, surviving everything
from the vacuum of space to the literal fires

00:04:14.989 --> 00:04:16.230
of Hell.

00:04:16.230 --> 00:04:21.339
Lobo can effortlessly go toe-to-toe with Superman
in a fight, and at one point he even gained

00:04:21.339 --> 00:04:25.770
the ability to make clones of himself from
a single drop of blood.

00:04:25.770 --> 00:04:32.669
How do you make a movie about an all-powerful
jerk who wears leather and rides a space motorcycle?

00:04:32.669 --> 00:04:36.819
Oh, yeah—Lobo rides a space motorcycle.

00:04:36.819 --> 00:04:38.370
Design throwback

00:04:38.370 --> 00:04:42.569
Lobo faces a unique problem when it comes
to modern appearances.

00:04:42.569 --> 00:04:47.689
The character was introduced in the 1980s,
and very quickly settled on his signature

00:04:47.689 --> 00:04:50.460
look: a leather-clad space biker.

00:04:50.460 --> 00:04:55.090
On Lobo's best day, he looks like an extra
from the original Mad Max movies.

00:04:55.090 --> 00:04:56.139
And on his worst?

00:04:56.139 --> 00:04:58.250
“At first I was scared ‘cause they looked
a little rough.

00:04:58.250 --> 00:04:59.580
I thought they were gonna beat me up.

00:04:59.580 --> 00:05:03.590
But they took me in their arms and told me
that I was a Bear too.”

00:05:03.590 --> 00:05:04.590
“How are ya?”

00:05:04.590 --> 00:05:10.939
And that might be problematic for the DC Extended
Universe as Warner Bros. tries to update the

00:05:10.939 --> 00:05:13.130
look of its heroes and villains.

00:05:13.130 --> 00:05:14.729
Don't ever change

00:05:14.729 --> 00:05:20.719
So, with all these issues — from a nutty
origin, to crazy powers, to dated fashion

00:05:20.719 --> 00:05:23.550
choices — why not just change him?

00:05:23.550 --> 00:05:26.300
Well, DC tried that already, too.

00:05:26.300 --> 00:05:30.699
When the publisher was busy reinventing its
heroes with visual and narrative revisions

00:05:30.699 --> 00:05:35.999
in the "New 52" event back in 2011, Lobo got
a makeover of his own.

00:05:35.999 --> 00:05:41.550
The result was a generic genre character,
who turned out to be the opposite of everything

00:05:41.550 --> 00:05:43.889
Lobo's fans actually loved.

00:05:43.889 --> 00:05:50.319
The outcry against the redesign was intense,
resulting in petitions, angry letters, and

00:05:50.319 --> 00:05:53.729
really angry internet comments from Lobo's
fans.

00:05:53.729 --> 00:05:59.080
If Warner Bros. sticks with the classic Lobo,
the movie is pretty much unmakeable.

00:05:59.080 --> 00:06:02.909
If they change him, Lobo fans will go berserk.

00:06:02.909 --> 00:06:05.039
Might as well not bother, right?

00:06:05.039 --> 00:06:06.050
Thanks for watching!

00:06:06.050 --> 00:06:09.129
Click the Looper icon to subscribe to our
YouTube channel.

00:06:09.129 --> 00:06:11.949
Plus check out all this cool stuff we know
you'll love, too.

